  "articleBody": "It's easy to overlook a small height difference between rooms, but sometimes, those floor level transitions really need a pro's touch. How do you know when to call in the experts? Firstly, if the level difference is pretty large, we're talking more than a slight bump, that's a clear signal. Trying to DIY a big height change can lead to an unstable or even unsafe transition. Secondly, if you suspect the subfloor might be moving, damaged, or uneven underneath, a professional eye is crucial. They can diagnose and fix the underlying issue, not just mask it. Thirdly, if that transition has become a trip hazard, it's not just annoying – it's a safety concern, especially for kids or older family members. A pro can ensure it's smoothed out properly. Finally, for any project in a commercial setting or an accessible route, where compliance and inspections are involved, you absolutely need a qualified professional. They understand the codes and can ensure everything passes muster. Don't risk it when safety and long-term durability are on the line; give us a call to chat about your options.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}